  Two things in it worth your attention specifically:

  - [1mThe degradation behavior.[0m A [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m throw (private mode, storage disabled, quota) silently falls back to an
    in-memory store for the life of the page, and [38;5;153mset[39m never surfaces an error to the caller. That means a user can check
    "Remember me", see no error, and find their username not remembered next visit. I chose silence because the
    alternative is an error on a login form for a non-essential feature — but it is a deliberate tradeoff, not an
    oversight.
  - [1mNo DOM tests.[0m The store is fully unit-tested through the injectable storage seam, but the [38;5;153mapp.js[39m/[38;5;153mindex.html[39m wiring —
    prefill, checkbox state, clear-on-uncheck — is verified manually. Adding jsdom would be the repo's first
    dependency, which your tooling answer ruled out.

